%S A123407 1,2,4,11,33,147,896,8683,131332,3065093,105578857,5179901931,
%T A123407 352226205662
%N A123407 Number of BIP* perfect graphs on n nodes.
%C A123407 A graph is BIP* if every induced nonbipartite subgraph H has a star cutset in H or in its complement. A star cutset is a set C whose deletion disconnects the graph and which contains a vertex adjacent to every other vertex of C (see Hougardy, 2006). All BIP* graphs are perfect. - _Meghanto Majumder_, Oct 05 2026
%H A123407 S. Hougardy, <a href="http://www.or.uni-bonn.de/~hougardy/">Home Page</a>
